<title>UK: British Airways monthly traffic statistics.</title>
<headline>British Airways monthly traffic statistics.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Wednesday its cargo tonne kilometres (CTKs) in February were up by 9.2 percent over the previous year resulting in total mainline scheduled revenue tonne kilometres (RTKs) increasing by 7.2 percent.</p>
<p>Detailed traffic statistics for February 1997 and for the first 11 eleven months of the financial year included:</p>
<p>FREIGHT TRAFFIC AND CAPACITY STATISTICS</p>
<p>				 FEBRUARY 1997	     APRIL-FEB</p>
<p>				 1997    1996   Pct    96/97   95/96 Pct    Change</p>
<p>Change</p>
<p> Freight tonne km (FTK)  305     279  up 9.2    3436    3160	   up 8.8</p>
<p> Total RTK		  1014     945  up 7.2   12757   11940	   up 6.8</p>
<p> Available tonne km     1486    1417  up 4.9   18216   16962	   up 7.4</p>
<p>TOTAL GROUP SCHEDULED SERVICES (including Deutsche BA, TAT)</p>
<p> Passengers carried     2710    2573  up 5.3   34060   32483	   up 4.9</p>
<p> Revenue passenger km   7342    6849  up 7.2   95323   89501	   up 6.5</p>
<p> Available seat km     10799   10281  up 5.0  131909  122817	   up 7.4</p>
<p> Total RTK (m)	    1030     959  up 7.4   12938   12092	   up 7.0</p>
<p> Available tonne km     1524    1451  up 5.1   18618   17308	   up 7.6</p>
<p>* ATK figures for mainline scheduled services for the previous year have been restated to reflect improved calculation methodology.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
